{%- comment -%}
  Hartwick Atelier — the binder rings on the homepage opening.

  Aloha's artboard binds the two hero photographs like the pages of a
  scrapbook: two chrome rings pass through punched holes either side of the
  seam. Cut from the artboard they would carry a patch of the artboard's
  photographs with them, so they are drawn here instead — one SVG, used
  twice, positioned by CSS on the seam at a quarter and three-quarters of
  the height (the artboard's 186 and 572 on a 769 frame). On a phone the
  frames stack and the rings turn with the seam.

  Decorative only: aria-hidden, no title. Colours are the artwork's own
  metal and paper, not tokens, in the same way the wordmark's are.

  Usage: {% render 'ha-home-rings' %}
{%- endcomment -%}

<span class="ha-home-hero__rings" aria-hidden="true">
  {%- for i in (1..2) -%}
    <svg class="ha-home-hero__ring ha-home-hero__ring--{{ i }}" viewBox="0 0 140 28" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" focusable="false">
      {%- if forloop.first -%}
        <defs>
          <linearGradient id="ha-ring-metal" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
            <stop offset="0" stop-color="#fdfcf8"/>
            <stop offset="0.35" stop-color="#d9d6cf"/>
            <stop offset="0.62" stop-color="#5e5952"/>
            <stop offset="0.85" stop-color="#8d887f"/>
            <stop offset="1" stop-color="#f1efe8"/>
          </linearGradient>
          <radialGradient id="ha-ring-hole" cx="0.5" cy="0.5" r="0.5">
            <stop offset="0" stop-color="#0b0603"/>
            <stop offset="0.72" stop-color="#1c1510"/>
            <stop offset="1" stop-color="#3a312a"/>
          </radialGradient>
        </defs>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- comment -%} the punched holes: paper rim, dark hole {%- endcomment -%}
      <circle cx="16" cy="14" r="11" fill="#f3f0e7" opacity="0.9"/>
      <circle cx="16" cy="14" r="8.5" fill="url(#ha-ring-hole)"/>
      <circle cx="124" cy="14" r="11" fill="#f3f0e7" opacity="0.9"/>
      <circle cx="124" cy="14" r="8.5" fill="url(#ha-ring-hole)"/>
      {%- comment -%} the ring: shadow, body, highlight {%- endcomment -%}
      <path d="M16 16 Q70 8 124 16" fill="none" stroke="#0b0603" stroke-opacity="0.35" stroke-width="7.5" stroke-linecap="round" transform="translate(0 1.5)"/>
      <path d="M16 15 Q70 7 124 15" fill="none" stroke="url(#ha-ring-metal)" stroke-width="6.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
      <path d="M18 13.2 Q70 5.8 122 13.2" fill="none" stroke="#ffffff" stroke-opacity="0.7" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round"/>
    </svg>
  {%- endfor -%}
</span>
